<!-- The NMIB motion and memorandum's Word styles: the cross-engine recipe (tools/fb/src/docxxengine.rs) in the face of
     the typst template ({font}, Times New Roman) at 12 pt (LR 5.2(a): a serif font of 12 point or larger; size 24
     half points); Body Text in exact 24 pt line boxes (typst pitch: the numbered lines, double spacing) with a
     half-inch first-line indent, the headings in them; the cover, the tables of contents and authorities and the
     signature in 12 pt boxes (typst pitch-single, two lines per numbered line). docx/nmib-motion-brief.lua writes every
     paragraph's own spacing, the three sections (the cover unnumbered, the tables in roman, the memorandum in arabic;
     letter, margins 1.5 in top and bottom, 1.3 in left, 1 in right) and their footers: the numbers 1 to 24 in a frame
     at the left of the numbered lines, the pleading rules the height of the page, the page number under the last
     numbered line (FORMBOOK_FOOTERS, FORMBOOK_FINAL). Twips: 20 x pt. -->
<reference xmlns:w="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main" xmlns:r="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships" base="xengine" size="24" body="480" single="240" indent="720" heading="480" heading-before="480" heading-after="0"/>
